WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.900
Okay, so I'm talking about Glance here, and I'm building this to help small teams keep track of the work that they're handing off to AI agents and their background jobs.

00:07.900 --> 00:14.560
And I think this is important because it's catching not only that jobs ran, but it's also checking that business expectations are met.

00:14.700 --> 00:19.360
So here I logged in, and I could see that I have some failing jobs here.

00:19.560 --> 00:20.880
So I have 98 are passing.

00:21.100 --> 00:23.200
I've acknowledged one warning and one failing.

00:23.340 --> 00:26.820
So if I dig into this, I could see these two that require my attention.

00:26.820 --> 00:32.940
So one, for my Psyched Music, it's telling me that the Buffer failed posts need to be cleared.

00:33.320 --> 00:40.320
So this is, I mean, I happen to know what this is, but it's saying that there was six failures and that this alert goes off when there's five or more.

00:40.700 --> 00:43.060
And it gives me, so it tells me exactly what's going on.

00:43.180 --> 00:46.080
I could actually see the remediation right here, what I need to do to fix it.

00:46.140 --> 00:51.860
And I could also just hit copy details, and it just gives me all the information about this monitor remediation and what's running it.

00:51.880 --> 00:54.100
So I could actually paste this into an agent to help me fix it.

00:54.100 --> 01:00.180
And if I jump in and look at the configuration here, I could actually see how it works.

01:00.240 --> 01:08.820
And basically, every time a job runs, a payload comes in, and I could configure whatever I want to look at based on that JSON payload that comes in with each of the checks.

01:09.040 --> 01:16.840
And I could set up different monitors to fail at different times, including whether a value is how it compares to what my expectation was.

01:17.060 --> 01:19.200
Or I could look at the average over some number of runs as well.

01:19.200 --> 01:24.100
So I could say, hey, I only want to make sure that this only has a total of five failures over the course of a week or something like that.

01:24.420 --> 01:29.760
And then once I'm happy with what's going on with the monitor, I could just acknowledge it, and it gets acknowledged and closed down.

01:30.240 --> 01:30.740
Here's another.

01:31.180 --> 01:32.420
Again, these are all demo ones I sent up.

01:32.440 --> 01:36.800
But here's another one where I actually have a job running that does a nightly refactor of the code base.

01:37.100 --> 01:38.100
And it failed for some reason.

01:38.100 --> 01:46.240
And the reason it's telling me it failed here is that it actually has a PR from a previous night that was sitting in GitHub waiting to be merged and wasn't merged.

01:46.340 --> 01:48.780
So I could actually use remediation to see what's going on.

01:48.820 --> 01:50.440
I could see that job is sitting right here.

01:50.520 --> 01:53.700
So I could go and merge that job, and then I could just acknowledge this alert as well.

01:53.780 --> 01:56.420
So now when I come into my dashboard, I see that everything's passing.

01:56.680 --> 01:58.200
And then this is, like, super easy to set up.

01:58.200 --> 01:58.320
So now I'm going to go and merge that job.
